[
    {
        "content": "<p>I have a proof that square matrices of RC-like coefficients form a order-closed topology. I was wondering if this result already exists or if there is a more canonical way of proving it.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">RCLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ComplexOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MatrixOrder</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrderClosedTopology</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">isClosed_le'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">change</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsClosed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">PosSemidef</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">PosSemidef</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsHermitian</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⋂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">star</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⬝ᵥ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*ᵥ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">ext</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_inter_iff</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_ofPred_eq</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_iInter</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">posSemidef_iff_dotProduct_mulVec</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsClosed</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isClosed_eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isClosed_iInter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isClosed_le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 613667499,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1785423375
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leansearch.net/?q=OrderClosedTopology+for+matrices\">Mathlib search</a> doesn't show it and quick <a href=\"https://loogle.lean-lang.org/?q=%22OrderClosedTopology%22\">Loogle search</a> doesn't show it either. So, I don't think it exist directly. However, for RCLike-matrices there is an equivalence between <code>Matrices</code> and <code>CStarMatrices</code>. <code>CStarMatrices</code> have a <code>CStarAlgebra</code> instance, and <code>CStarAlgebras</code> have <code>OrderClosedTopology</code> instances. So, one could argue it is there indirectly. </p>\n<p>I am not familiar enough with the design decisions on <code>Matrices</code> and <code>CStarMatrices</code> to comment on whether it is a worthwhile contribution.</p>\n<p>I see that your implementation requires <code>[Fintype n]</code>. PSD matrices are defined for arbitrary index sets, so I am not sure you need that restriction.</p>",
        "id": 613807370,
        "sender_full_name": "Tjeerd Jan Heeringa",
        "timestamp": 1785484708
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This proof requires <code>[Fintype n]</code> because it uses <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/PosDef.html#Matrix.posSemidef_iff_dotProduct_mulVec\">Matrix.posSemidef_iff_dotProduct_mulVec</a>, but actually you can just directly expand the definition of <code>PosSemidef</code> to get </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsHermitian</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⋂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">star</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xj</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which is still an intersection of closed sets and hence <code>OrderClosedTopology (Matrix n n 𝕜)</code> holds without <code>[Fintype n]</code>.</p>\n<p>But also notice that if you only care about it for <code>ℂ</code> the following version already exists in Mathlib (as mentioned by <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"983090\">@Tjeerd Jan Heeringa</span> ), but it does not work for an arbitrary <code>RCLike 𝕜</code> as we only have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Analysis/CStarAlgebra/Matrix.html#Matrix.instCStarAlgebra\">Matrix.instCStarAlgebra</a>: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Analysis</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Order</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Analysis</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CStarAlgebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousFunctionalCalculus</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Order</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">RCLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ComplexOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MatrixOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Norms</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">L2Operator</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrderClosedTopology</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">failed to synthesize</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">substring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrderClosedTopology</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 613823799,
        "sender_full_name": "Yongxi Lin (Aaron)",
        "timestamp": 1785490802
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks a lot for your help <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"983090\">@Tjeerd Jan Heeringa</span> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"669043\">@Yongxi Lin (Aaron)</span>! I successfully removed the <code>[Fintype n]</code> assumption. I only care about <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6889em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbb\">R</span></span></span></span> for my application but I believe that a general instance is valuable. I'm just wondering if it won't be an issue to have both instances for <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6889em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbb\">C</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<p>Here is the updated version:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">RCLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span 